{"answer":"During the November 2025 us-east incident where streaming chat responses were dropping, a customer (Lattice Financial) reported intermittent 5xx errors and stream resets affecting the /v1/chat/completions endpoint with stream=true in the us-east region from approximately 16:05 to 16:35 UTC, with some residual retries for another 10 minutes. The Redwood public status page incorrectly showed 'Operational' during this timeframe because the status page components were too coarse (only Hosted API global) and lacked the granularity to reflect streaming-specific and region-specific degradation properly. 

An internal incident (INC-2025-1107-USE1-STREAMING) confirmed the streaming degradation starting at ~16:09 UTC and mitigation by 16:34 UTC, with monitoring continuing through 16:50 UTC. The delayed and ambiguous external communications were due to the incomplete signal mapping and inability to represent streaming (us-east) separately from the global Hosted API component.

The support and SRE teams provided a written acknowledgement and corrected timeline to the customer explaining the status page mismatch was due to component granularity limitations. They committed to improvements including finer component granularity by product surface and region, standardized incident communication templates, and faster update processes. A short post-incident summary was to be published once reviewed for confidentiality. The customer accepted this explanation and the incident was closed with follow-ups integrated into a status page transparency upgrades initiative.","document_ids":["dsid_1eba87b0b11b4f31a006f0cf164b8509"]}
